# Allowlist for scripts/forbidden_words.py (plan: one reviewed exception per line).
#
#   <path glob> | <rule id, matched text or *> | <reason>
#
# * The glob is matched against the path from the repository root; "*" also crosses folders.
# * The term is a rule id (python3 scripts/forbidden_words.py --list-rules), the exact matched
#   text (for example one store domain), "placeholder", "template-hint", "email" or "*" (any rule
#   except "email"). Terms from the private list (--extra-terms) can never be excused.
# * "@name" as the path covers the name check (repository, package and README title names).
# * Every entry needs a reason a reviewer can check. Scope entries to data or UI files, or to the
#   one domain the project really links to. A funding file can never be allowlisted.
# * Unused entries are reported as warnings; delete them.

scripts/forbidden_words.py | * | the check's own rule list, its documentation and the usage examples
tests/test_forbidden_words.py | * | test sentences that must trigger the rules
tests/test_check_pr_title.py | * | test titles that must be rejected for their wording
scripts/set_byline.py | placeholder | prints the names of the placeholders to fill again after a brand swap
LICENSE | sell | the licence grants the right to "sell copies" of the software
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md | sell | the unchanged MIT notice of the create-expo-app scaffold grants the right to "sell copies"
package-lock.json | funding | npm copies each dependency's "funding" metadata into the lockfile; generated, not project text
package-lock.json | funding-platform | the same npm metadata holds third-party maintainers' funding URLs; none of them is ours
package-lock.json | sponsor | the same npm metadata contains github.com/sponsors URLs of third-party maintainers
package-lock.json | buy | npm copies the deprecation notice of glob 7 ("may be purchased") into the lockfile; machine-generated, not project text
package-lock.json | email | the same glob 7 deprecation notice carries its maintainer's address; machine-generated, not project text
assets/fonts/Sora-OFL.txt | sell | the unchanged SIL Open Font License text grants the right to sell the font
assets/fonts/Sora-OFL.txt | product-host | the unchanged SIL Open Font License text links scripts.sil.org, the licence's home
